# Deny everything, then allow back only what the build actually needs.
#
# An allow-list rather than a deny-list on purpose: with a deny-list, every new
# file or directory added to the repo silently joins the build context, and the
# failure mode is leaking something (a .sql snapshot, credentials, notes) into
# an image layer. Here, anything new is excluded until explicitly permitted.
*

!package.json
!package-lock.json
!src/

# NOTE: there are deliberately no re-exclusions under src/ any more. Tests and
# fixtures used to live there and needed `src/**/*.test.js` and
# `src/**/__fixtures__/` to keep them out of the zip -- an enumeration that
# covered those two shapes and nothing else, so a helper module or a second
# fixture directory would have shipped. They now live in test/, which the `*`
# rule above denies without being named. Same for tools/.
#
# The rule to keep: if it is under src/, it ships. Put anything that should not
# ship somewhere else rather than adding a pattern here.
**/node_modules/
**/.DS_Store
